          "text": "Sure \u2014 here\u2019s a reliable, classic lasagne recipe (serves 6\u20138) with options for b\u00e9chamel or ricotta, plus a vegetarian swap and make-ahead/freezing tips.\n\nTimes\n- Prep: 30\u201345 minutes (longer if you make sauce from scratch)\n- Cook: 45\u201350 minutes\n- Rest: 15 minutes\n\nIngredients (classic meat version)\n- Olive oil 1\u20132 tbsp\n- 1 medium onion, finely chopped\n- 2\u20133 garlic cloves, minced\n- 1 lb (450 g) ground beef (or 50/50 beef+pork ~1 lb total)\n- Salt & pepper\n- 1/2 cup (120 ml) dry red wine (optional)\n- 1 (28 oz / 800 g) can crushed tomatoes\n- 2 tbsp tomato paste\n- 1 tsp dried oregano, 1 tsp dried basil (or 1 tbsp fresh chopped)\n- 1 tsp sugar (optional, to balance acidity)\n- 9\u201312 lasagne noodles (regular or no-boil, depending on pan size; a 9x13 inch pan typically uses 9\u201312)\n- 2 cups (200\u2013250 g) shredded mozzarella\n- 1 cup (100 g) grated Parmesan or Pecorino\n\nB\u00e9chamel (white sauce) option\n- 4 tbsp (60 g) butter\n- 4 tbsp (30 g) all-purpose flour\n- 3 cups (700 ml) milk, warmed\n- Pinch nutmeg, salt, pepper\n\nRicotta option (instead of b\u00e9chamel)\n- 15 oz (425 g) ricotta\n- 1 large egg\n- 1 cup (100 g) grated Parmesan\n- 2 tbsp chopped parsley or basil, salt & pepper\n\nVegetarian swap\n- Replace meat with about 1 lb (450 g) mixture of chopped mushrooms + zucchini + spinach, or use 1\u20132 cups cooked lentils. Saut\u00e9 until soft and proceed same as meat sauce.\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Make the sauce\n   - Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat. Saut\u00e9 onion until translucent, add garlic 30 sec.\n   - Add ground meat, season, brown and break up. If using veg, saut\u00e9 until soft.\n   - Optional: add wine, simmer 2\u20133 min to reduce.\n   - Stir in tomato paste, crushed tomatoes, herbs, sugar. Simmer 20\u201330 minutes (longer for deeper flavor). Adjust salt/pepper.\n\n2. Prepare b\u00e9chamel or ricotta\n   - B\u00e9chamel: melt butter, whisk in flour to form roux; cook 1\u20132 min; slowly whisk in warm milk until smooth and thickened; finish with salt, pepper, pinch nutmeg.\n   - Ricotta mix: combine ricotta, egg, Parmesan, parsley, salt & pepper.\n\n3. Preheat oven to 375\u00b0F (190\u00b0C).\n\n4. Assemble (9x13-inch pan)\n   - Spread a thin layer (about 1 cup) of sauce on bottom.\n   - Lay 3\u20134 noodles in a single layer (trim if needed).\n   - Spread a portion of ricotta mixture or a thin layer of b\u00e9chamel.\n   - Spoon a layer of meat sauce, sprinkle some mozzarella and a little Parmesan.\n   - Repeat: noodles \u2192 cheese/b\u00e9chamel \u2192 sauce \u2192 cheese. Finish with a final layer of noodles (optional), sauce on top and a generous sprinkle of mozzarella + Parmesan.\n\n   Notes:\n   - If using no-boil noodles, ensure there\u2019s a bit more sauce (or a splash of water/milk) so noodles can soften.\n   - Aim for 3 layers of noodles for best structure.\n\n5. Bake\n   - Cover loosely with foil (spray underside with oil so it won\u2019t stick).\n   - Bake covered 25 minutes, remove foil, bake 20\u201325 minutes more until bubbling and top is golden.\n   - If using no-boil noodles, add ~10 minutes to covered time.\n\n6. Rest & serve\n   - Remove from oven and let rest 15 minutes before cutting so it sets. Serve with a salad or garlic bread.\n\nMake-ahead & freezing\n- Assemble and refrigerate (covered) up to 24 hours before baking.\n- Freeze assembled (unbaked): wrap tightly; freeze up to 2\u20133 months. Bake from frozen: increase covered baking time by ~20\u201330 minutes, then uncover and brown.\n- Refrigerated leftovers last 3\u20134 days. Reheat covered in oven at 350\u00b0F (175\u00b0C) until heated through, or microwave slices.\n\nTips\n- Drain excess fat from meat if too greasy before adding tomatoes.\n- For richer flavor, simmer sauce longer (45\u201360 minutes) and use some fresh basil at the end.\n- For extra creaminess, add a little b\u00e9chamel between layers even if using ricotta.\n- Let it rest \u2014 slicing too soon makes a sloppy lasagne.\n\nIf you want, I can give:\n- A fully vegetarian recipe with exact vegetable quantities and spices\n- A gluten-free or low-carb (zucchini- or eggplant-sliced) version\n- A scaled recipe for smaller/larger pans\n\nWhich would you like?"
